#
# The independent SHA-2 implementations this project compares against: the
# oracles of the differential tests (tests/validation, "Oracles") and the
# baselines of the benchmarks (bench/). Shell syntax, read by build.sh.
#
# Each source is a release archive pinned by its SHA-256; the full commit
# it was made from is recorded beside it. OpenSSL is the only project that
# publishes a checksum for its archive, and the one below matches it.
# BoringSSL and SPHINCS+ have no release to pin, so their archives are the
# ones GitHub makes of a commit.

OPENSSL_NAME=openssl-4.0.3
OPENSSL_URL=https://github.com/openssl/openssl/releases/download/openssl-4.0.3/openssl-4.0.3.tar.gz
OPENSSL_SHA256=325b5c806167c13b40b1ffeadfe0248197c00eccc4cf123ec1e28d2d2fd216d9
OPENSSL_COMMIT=af1775b60dfa141a4ad762585052cabeb9f37e9e

